15	    ///
16	    /// This rule checks for duplicate selectors across a stylesheet. A duplicate
17	    /// occurs when two rules have the same fully-resolved selector list (after
18	    /// sorting for order-independence), within the same at-rule context.
19	    ///
20	    /// Selectors are **normalized** before comparison so that equivalent selectors
21	    /// written differently are still caught:
22	    /// - Whitespace differences are ignored.
23	    /// - HTML type selectors are compared case-insensitively (`DIV` == `div`).
24	    /// - Compound selector parts are order-normalized, so `.a.b` and `.b.a` are
25	    ///   considered equal.
26	    /// - Selector list order is ignored: `.a, .b` and `.b, .a` are equal.
27	    ///
28	    /// CSS nesting is fully resolved before comparison:
29	    /// `a { & b {} }` produces the resolved selector `a b`, which is compared
30	    /// against all other resolved selectors in the same context.
31	    ///
32	    /// Selectors are only compared within the same at-rule context. A selector
33	    /// inside `@media` is not considered a duplicate of the same selector at the
34	    /// top level.
35	    ///
36	    /// ## Examples
37	    ///
38	    /// ### Invalid
39	    ///
40	    /// ```css,expect_diagnostic
41	    /// .foo {}
